# TEMPORARY: the stack is pinned at a fork, not at OPCFoundation.
#
# The pinned commit carries three fixes we depend on that are not yet on
# upstream master. Two live in open pull request #4195:
#
#   * DataGenerator.GetRandomNodeId returning NodeId.Null when boundary
#     values were not requested (issue #4226)
#   * Opc.Ua.Mcp.Core made trim and Native AOT clean (was PR #4228)
#
# The third is a security fix found reviewing the MCP integration:
#
#   * CaptureSessionManager.StartAsync validated SessionFolder but passed
#     PcapFilePath and KeyLogFilePath through verbatim, which made the MCP
#     start_capture tool an arbitrary file read and overwrite primitive.
#     Reported upstream; not yet merged.
#
# Those commits exist only in the fork, and CI checks out submodules with
# actions/checkout plus submodules: recursive, which fetches from the url
# below. Leaving it pointed at OPCFoundation would fail the checkout,
# because refs/pull/4195/head is not fetched by that action.
#
# REVERT THIS once all three have landed upstream: put the url back to
# https://github.com/OPCFoundation/UA-.NETStandard.git, set branch to
# master, and repin to upstream master. CI refuses to publish images or
# NuGet packages while this points anywhere but OPCFoundation, so a
# forgotten revert fails the build rather than shipping.
#
#   https://github.com/OPCFoundation/UA-.NETStandard/pull/4195
#
[submodule "external/UA-.NETStandard"]
	path = external/UA-.NETStandard
	url = https://github.com/marcschier/UA-.NETStandard.git
	branch = marcschier/capture-artifact-path-validation
